   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "def sor_iteration_matrix(A, omega):\n",
    "    L = np.tril(A, -1)\n",
    "    U = np.triu(A, 1)\n",
    "    D = A - L - U\n",
    "    return np.dot(np.linalg.inv(D + omega * L), ((1 - omega) * D - omega * U))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define coefficient matrix\n",
    "A = np.array([[4, 3, 0], [3, 4, -1], [0, -1, 4]])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Loop through values of omega and calculate the spectral radius of the iteration matrix\n",
    "omega = np.arange(0, 2 + 1e-4, 1e-4)\n",
    "rho = np.zeros(omega.shape)\n",
    "for i in range(len(omega)):\n",
    "    T_SOR = sor_iteration_matrix(A, omega[i])\n",
    "    rho[i] = max(abs(np.linalg.eigvals(T_SOR)))\n",
    "    \n",
    "# Plot spectral radii\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6,4))\n",
    "plt.plot(omega, rho, \"b\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"$\\omega$\", fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.ylabel(r\"$\\rho(T_{SOR})$\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "edd07022",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Here we can see that the optimum value of $\\omega$ is approximately $\\omega = 1.25$\n",
    "\n",
    "## Theorem: Optimum Relaxation Parameter\n",
    "\n",
    "If a system of linear equations of the form $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ has a coefficient matrix $A$ with all real eigenvalues then the optimum relaxation parameter for the SOR method can be calculated using\n",
    "\n",
    "$$ \\omega_{opt} = 1+{\\left(\\frac{\\rho (T_J )}{1+\\sqrt{1-\\rho (T_J )^2 }}\\right)}^2, $$\n",
    "\n",
    "where $\\rho(T_J)$ is the spectral radius of the iteration matrix of the Jacobi method.\n",
    "\n",
    "We saw in the previous example that the spectral radius of the iteration matrix for the Jacobi method for the system is $\\rho(T_J )=0.7906$, so\n",
    "\n",
    "$$ \\begin{align*}\n",
    "    \\omega = 1 + \\left( \\frac{0.7906}{1 + \\sqrt{1 - 0.7906)^2}} \\right)^2 \\approx 1.2404.\n",
    "\\end{align*} $$\n",
    "\n",
    "## SOR Method: Example 7.5\n",
    "\n",
    "Solve the system of linear equations shown below using the SOR method with $\\omega = 1.24$ and an accuracy tolerance of $tol = 10^{-4}$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$ \\begin{align*}\n",
    "    4x_1 +3x_2 &=-2,\\\\\n",
    "    3x_1 +4x_2 -x_3 &=-8,\\\\\n",
    "    -x_2 +4x_3 &=14.\n",
    "\\end{align*} $$\n",
    "\n",
    ":::{.fragment}\n",
    "**Solution**: The SOR method for this system is\n",
    "\n",
    "$$ \\begin{align*}\n",
    "    x_{1}^{(k+1)} &= (1 - \\omega)x_{1}^{(k)} + \\frac{\\omega}{4} \\left( -2 - 3 x_{2}^{(k)} \\right), \\\\\n",
    "    x_{2}^{(k+1)} &= (1 - \\omega)x_{2}^{(k)} + \\frac{\\omega}{4} \\left( -8 - 3 x_{1}^{(k+1)} + x_{3}^{(k)} \\right), \\\\\n",
    "    x_{3}^{(k+1)} &= (1 - \\omega)x_{3}^{(k)} + \\frac{\\omega}{4} \\left( 14 + x_{2}^{(k+1)} \\right).\n",
    "\\end{align*} $$\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "Using starting values of $\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{0}$. Calculating the first iteration\n",
    "\n",
    "$$ \\begin{align*}\n",
    "    x_{1}^{(1)} &= (1 - 1.24)(-0.5) + \\frac{1.24}{4} \\left( -2 - 3 (-1.625) \\right) = -0.5, \\\\\n",
    "    x_{2}^{(1)} &= (1 - 1.24)(-1.625) + \\frac{1.24}{4} \\left( -8 - 3 (-0.5) + -3.09375 \\right) = -1.625, \\\\\n",
    "    x_{3}^{(1)} &= (1 - 1.24)(3.09375) + \\frac{1.24}{4} \\left( 14 + 1.625 \\right) = 3.09375.\n",
    "\\end{align*} $$\n",
    "\n",
    "Calculate the residual\n",
    "\n",
    "$$ \\begin{align*}\n",
    "    \\mathbf{r}^{(1)} &= \\mathbf{b} - A \\mathbf{x}^{(1)} = \n",
    "    \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 14 \\end{pmatrix} -\n",
    "    \\begin{pmatrix} 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4 \\end{pmatrix}\n",
    "    \\begin{pmatrix} -0.5 \\\\ -1.625 \\\\ 3.09375 \\end{pmatrix}\n",
    "    =\n",
    "    \\begin{pmatrix} 4.875 \\\\ 3.09375 \\\\ 0.0 \\end{pmatrix}.\n",
    "\\end{align*} $$\n",
    "\n",
    "Since $\\max(| \\mathbf{r}^{(1)} |) = 4.875 > 10^{-4}$ we continue iterating.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "Calculating the second iteration\n",
    "\n",
    "$$ \\begin{align*}\n",
    "    x_{1}^{(2)} &= (1 - 1.24)(0.71875) + \\frac{1.24}{4} \\left( -2 - 3 (-1.765625) \\right) = 0.71875, \\\\\n",
    "    x_{2}^{(2)} &= (1 - 1.24)(-1.765625) + \\frac{1.24}{4} \\left( -8 - 3 (0.71875) + -3.05859375 \\right) \\\\\n",
    "    &= -1.765625, \\\\\n",
    "    x_{3}^{(2)} &= (1 - 1.24)(3.05859375)+  \\frac{1.24}{4} \\left( 14 + 1.765625 \\right) = 3.05859375.\n",
    "\\end{align*} $$\n",
    "\n",
    "Calculate the residual\n",
    "\n",
    "$$ \\begin{align*}\n",
    "    \\mathbf{r}^{(2)} &= \\mathbf{b} - A \\mathbf{x}^{(1)} = \n",
    "    \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 14 \\end{pmatrix} -\n",
    "    \\begin{pmatrix} 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4 \\end{pmatrix}\n",
    "    \\begin{pmatrix} 0.71875 \\\\ -1.765625 \\\\ 3.05859375 \\end{pmatrix}\n",
    "    =\n",
    "    \\begin{pmatrix} 0.421875 \\\\ -0.03515625 \\\\ 0.0 \\end{pmatrix}.\n",
    "\\end{align*} $$\n",
    "\n",
    "Since $\\max(| \\mathbf{r}^{(2)} |) = 0.421875 > 10^{-4}$ we continue iterating. \n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "The SOR method was iterated until $\\max(|\\mathbf{r}|) < 10^{-4}$ and the iteration values are given in the table below. \n",
    "\n",
    "| $k$ |  $x_{1}$  |  $x_{2}$  |  $x_{3}$  | $\\max(| \\mathbf{r} |)$ |\n",
    "|:---:|:---------:|:---------:|:---------:|:---------:|\n",
    "|   0 |  0.000000 |  0.000000 |  0.000000 | 14.000000 |\n",
    "|   1 | -0.620000 | -1.903400 |  3.749946 |  6.19e+00 |\n",
    "|   2 |  1.298962 | -2.068735 |  2.798705 |  9.90e-01 |\n",
    "|   3 |  0.992173 | -2.038626 |  3.036337 |  2.14e-01 |\n",
    "|   4 |  1.037801 | -2.014620 |  2.986747 |  1.07e-01 |\n",
    "|   5 |  1.004524 | -2.004807 |  3.001690 |  1.16e-02 |\n",
    "|   6 |  1.003385 | -2.001470 |  2.999139 |  9.13e-03 |\n",
    "|   7 |  1.000555 | -2.000430 |  3.000073 |  9.29e-04 |\n",
    "|   8 |  1.000267 | -2.000122 |  2.999944 |  7.01e-04 |\n",
    "|   9 |  1.000050 | -2.000034 |  3.000003 |  9.65e-05 |\n",
    "\n",
    "The SOR method took 9 iterations to achieve convergence to $tol=10^{-4}$ whereas the Jacobi method took 49 iterations and the Gauss-Seidel method took 19 iterations to achieve the same accuracy.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Indirect methods** use an iterative approach to calculate estimates of the solution.\n",
    "- The **Jacobi method** rearranges each equation to make the diagonal element the subject.\n",
    "- The **Gauss-Seidel method** improves the Jacobi method by using new estimates in the calculations when they are available.\n",
    "- The **iteration matrix** is a matrix $T$ such that $\\mathbf{x}^{(k+1)} = T\\mathbf{x}^{(k)} + \\mathbf{c}$.\n",
    "- An indirect method converges if the **spectral radius** of the iteration matrix, $\\rho(T)$, is less than 1.\n",
    "- The smaller the value of $\\rho(T)$, the quicker the method will converge.\n",
    "- The **SOR** method improves on the convergence Gauss-Seidel method by amplifying or slowing down the Gauss-Seidel method. "
   ]
  }
